<title>USA: U.S. CASH SOYMEAL - SOYMEAL BASIS OFFERS WEAKEN.</title>
<headline>U.S. CASH SOYMEAL - SOYMEAL BASIS OFFERS WEAKEN.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis offers for soymeal in truck and rail markets fell Monday as dealers attempt to sell larger volumes of soymeal before the August option expires, they said.</p>
<p>&quot;People are willing to discount the basis versus August rather than sell it against the September,&quot; a crusher from the southeast said.</p>
<p>August holds an approximate 25.00-cent-per-ton premium to September, but the August contract expires on August 20.</p>
<p>Dealers also said supplies of soymeal were ample because a falling soybean basis has prompted a moderate to heavy crush.</p>
<p>&quot;Those (crushers) that are going down have been crushing pretty hard lately,&quot; said one broker. &quot;They want to make sure supply is good when they're down.&quot;  </p>
